From: pomme kernel stage
Subject: [PATCH] backlight: apple_pmic_bl: add default case to get_brightness

GCC 15 (Bootlin aarch64 2026.08-1, gcc 15.3.0) rejects
drivers/video/backlight/apple_pmic_bl.c with
"error: control reaches end of non-void function [-Werror=return-type]":
apple_pmic_bl_get_brightness()'s switch over data->type has no default
case, and C enums are ints, so control can fall off the end.

The postmarketOS flavor builds this file with clang (LLVM=1), which does
not flag it there; pomme builds with the pinned GCC toolchain.

Minimal fix: return 0 (backlight off) for an out-of-range PMIC type.
No behavior change for the two defined PMIC types (Anya, Aria).

Generated with git diff (hunk -64,6 +64,8, function context in header).
NOTE on hunk anchoring: a hand-anchored variant of this same change at
hunk header -62,7 +62,9 (5 leading / 2 trailing context lines, counts
matching the body) is byte-correct but GNU patch 2.7.6 refuses it
(reports "Hunk #1 FAILED at 62"; aligns only "with fuzz 2"), while the
git generated -64,6 +64,8 form applies cleanly. The requirement is that
the patch applies under BOTH plain "patch -p1 --dry-run" and
"git apply --check"; both verified for this file.

Verified against HoolockLinux/linux @ dfa4d42081312dd34ec33ee8d23174309f683188.
---
diff --git a/drivers/video/backlight/apple_pmic_bl.c b/drivers/video/backlight/apple_pmic_bl.c
index 64d472512..42029d9c5 100644
--- a/drivers/video/backlight/apple_pmic_bl.c
+++ b/drivers/video/backlight/apple_pmic_bl.c
@@ -64,6 +64,8 @@ static int apple_pmic_bl_get_brightness(struct backlight_device *bl)
 			return (cmd[0] << 3) | (cmd[1] & 7);
 		case PMIC_TYPE_ARIA:
 			return ((cmd[1] & 7) << 8) | (cmd[0] & 0xff);
+		default:
+			return 0;
 	}
 }
 
